# What must never end up inside a generated, committed artifact.
#
# graphify has two modes and only one of them is safe here. `graphify . --code-only` indexes the
# AST and nothing else — that is how graphify-out/ has always been built, and it is what `batten
# doctor` tells you to run. Plain `graphify update .` also indexes docs, and GRAPH_REPORT.md's own
# "next steps" line recommends exactly that. Run it once and docs/field-test lands inside
# graph.json and graph.html: 328 references, verbatim.
#
# That matters more than it looks, for two reasons. The field-test notes describe a private
# project, and the CI guard against tracked personal paths EXCLUDES graphify-out — a machine-
# generated 2 MB JSON is unreviewable in a diff, which is the same reason .gitattributes marks it
# linguist-generated. So a generated file is the one place where something private can be
# committed and no human or check will ever see it.
docs/field-test/

# Personal working material. Same rule as .gitignore, restated here because a graph is built from
# the working tree, not from the index — an untracked file is still fair game for the extractor.
*.local.md
*.pdf
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
